       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg is far above the 200 mg/day maximum, and a family visit or evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for it. I can't see a way to give this dose safely to a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 50 mg PO once daily, or up to 200 mg/day if the patient is already established on sertraline. Tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or a psychiatry consult.** If you think this patient needs something outside standard dosing, they can review it before anything is ordered. That can usually be done quickly.\n- **Add a note to the order.** I can include a note such as \"dose titration plan to be discussed at evening rounds.\"\n\nIf the goal is to have things settled by evening, starting a standard dose now and discussing the plan on rounds should meet that goal. Which of these would you like?"
